OL,3,ABaby orangutans found in Indian forest
OL,4,Aspark trafficking inquiry
OL,5,
OL,6,FFive baby orangutans have been found in
OL,7,Fa forest in India's eastern state of
OL,8,FOdisha, far from their natural habitat,
OL,9,Fprompting an investigation into how
OL,10,Fthey got there.
OL,12,FPhotographs and videos widely shared
OL,13,Fonline show the young apes sitting
OL,14,Ftogether on the forest floor and eating
OL,15,Fbananas, thousands of kilometres from
OL,16,Fthe tropical rainforests where they
OL,17,Fbelong.
OL,19,FOrangutans are not native to India. The
OL,20,Fcritically endangered apes are found in
OL,21,Fthe wild only in Indonesia and
OL,22,FMalaysia.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
